# Code owners for the paths that gate everything else (MDRS-49).
#
# STATUS: ADVISORY, NOT ENFORCED. The "main protection" ruleset on this repo
# (id 20827887) requires a pull request with 1 approval and the "Verify" and
# "Commit hygiene" status checks, but it does NOT set
# `require_code_owner_review`. So today this file only auto-requests these
# reviewers; any single approval still satisfies the rule. Turning it into a
# requirement is a repo-settings change, made deliberately and separately.
#
# These paths are the ones that can disable the other gates — a change to
# .github/ can drop a required check, a change to tools/ci/ can make a gate pass
# vacuously — so review of them must never be single-threaded on one person's
# availability.
#
# THE OWNER IS A TEAM, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING (MDRS-54).
#
# @amel-tech/medaris is the 9 write-or-above collaborators, and it holds `write`
# on this repository — a team without repository access silently voids the rule
# it appears in, exactly like naming a user who is not a collaborator.
#
# Naming the team rather than individuals is not cosmetic. Individual owners are
# ALL requested on every matching pull request, so a list long enough to survive
# one person's holiday is also long enough to spam everyone on every CI tweak.
# The team is paired with GitHub's CODE REVIEW ASSIGNMENT, configured on the team
# itself: round-robin, 2 reviewers per pull request, "notify entire team" OFF. So
# a matching pull request pings two people, the next one pings the next two, and
# nobody has to curate this file as staff change.
#
# ⚠ THE SETTING AND THIS FILE ARE COUPLED, AND THE SETTING IS NOT IN THE REPO.
# If code review assignment is ever disabled on the team, GitHub falls back to
# requesting the WHOLE team — 8 notifications per pull request instead of 2, with
# nothing here to warn you. Check it at
# https://github.com/orgs/amel-tech/teams/medaris/settings, or read it with:
#   gh api graphql -f query='query { organization(login:"amel-tech")
#     { team(slug:"medaris") { reviewRequestDelegationEnabled
#       reviewRequestDelegationMemberCount reviewRequestDelegationNotifyTeam } } }'
#
# WHY NOT A HAND-PICKED LIST. Measured across the full history of
# .github/workflows/: Taha 26 commits, safakadir 25, Samet 12, Onurkan 9, Enes 7,
# zahidcakici 4. The two-name list this replaced named neither the second nor the
# third most active person, and it named @tahaayan — Taha authors pull requests
# as @EsTharian, and because both are his real accounts GitHub never recognised
# the author as an owner and never skipped him. A team has neither failure mode.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching rule, so order is specific-after-general.

# Everything else has no owner: reviewer choice stays open for ordinary app and
# library work, which is where most PRs land.

# CI workflows, PR template, dependabot config, and this file itself.
/.github/ @amel-tech/medaris

# The gate scripts CI executes. Weakening one of these is indistinguishable
# from deleting the check it backs.
/tools/ci/ @amel-tech/medaris
